  "id": "initial-data-analysis",
  "term": "initial data analysis",
  "definition": "Initial data analysis is the stage after data have been gathered and before the main research-question analysis begins, used to build a dependable understanding of the dataset. It typically involves checking and describing data properties, documenting what is found, and, if needed, refining the planned analysis so the research is more transparent, reproducible, and valid.",
